    11	  `bool` is an `int` subtype, with `False`/`True` contributing `0`/`1`.
    12	- `Float` inputs range symbolically over the full K `Float` sort and cause the
    13	  function to return `false` before arithmetic is evaluated.
    14	
    15	If all three inputs pass `isinstance(_, int)`, the return value is true exactly
    16	when one input equals the sum of the other two. If any input is a `Float`, the
    17	return value is false. The final configuration also requires the module and
    18	builtin scopes, environment, scope allocator, heap, heap allocator, stack,
    19	return state, exception state, and exit code to equal their initial values.
